 ## Run many projects in parallel
 
-A [Cursor Project](https://cursor.com/blog/projects) gives one coordinator agent a persistent thread. The coordinator doesn't write code. It directs subagents, which run in the cloud by default, so the work continues when your laptop is closed. That's the shape the Orchestrate playbook expects. Start your prompts to the coordinator with `/n-mode`, and the subagents it spawns follow the playbooks.
+Give one coordinator chat the whole body of work. The coordinator doesn't write code. It directs subagents, each in its own worktree. Subagents stop when the session ends, so keep the machine awake for a long run. That's the shape the Orchestrate playbook expects. Start your prompts to the coordinator with `/n-mode`, and the subagents it spawns follow the playbooks.
 
 A few habits help:
 
-- Give each body of work its own Project, such as a feature, a migration, a perf push, or a tech-debt cleanup. Several can run side by side.
-- Drag related chats into the Project, finished ones included. They become context for every agent in it.
